{
  "id": "22145_kinshisuru",
  "headword": "{禁止|きんし}する",
  "reading": "きんしする",
  "romaji": "kinshisuru",
  "part_of_speech": "suru verb",
  "gloss": "to prohibit; to ban; to forbid",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to prohibit; to ban; to forbid",
      "explanation": "To officially or authoritatively prevent something from being done. Used for rules, laws, regulations, and formal restrictions."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "22145_kinshisuru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{喫煙|きつえん}を{禁止|きんし}する。",
      "english": "To prohibit smoking.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "22145_kinshisuru_ex2",
      "japanese": "この{公園|こうえん}では{犬|いぬ}の{散歩|さんぽ}が{禁止|きんし}されている。",
      "english": "Walking dogs is prohibited in this park.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "22145_kinshisuru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{政府|せいふ}は{未成年者|みせいねんしゃ}の{飲酒|いんしゅ}を{法律|ほうりつ}で{禁止|きんし}している。",
      "english": "The government prohibits minors from drinking alcohol by law.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A very common verb used for official prohibitions and bans. The noun form {禁止|きんし} is frequently seen on signs and in rules.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {喫煙|きつえん}{禁止|きんし}: no smoking\n- {駐車|ちゅうしゃ}{禁止|きんし}: no parking\n- {立入|たちいり}{禁止|きんし}: no entry\n- {使用|しよう}を{禁止|きんし}する: to prohibit use\n- {法律|ほうりつ}で{禁止|きんし}する: to prohibit by law\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {禁|きん}じる: to forbid — more literary and formal; used in written language\n- {制限|せいげん}する: to restrict — limits rather than completely bans\n- {規制|きせい}する: to regulate — controls through rules rather than outright banning\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\nOften used in the passive form {禁止|きんし}されている to describe a standing prohibition. The noun {禁止|きんし} alone is commonly seen on signs without する.",
